{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) assigned a stitch task (#5223) to implement srd008-ls requirements R4.1 through R4.4 in the go-unix-utils project. These requirements cover:\n   - R4.1: Exit 0 when all listed paths are accessed and output written successfully\n   - R4.2: Exit 1 when a minor problem occurs (permission denied, file not found), still list remaining accessible entries, print diagnostic to stderr\n   - R4.3: Exit 2 when a serious problem occurs (invalid command-line option)\n   - R4.4: Install SIGPIPE handler at startup via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   \n   The task requires modifying `cmd/ls/main.go` and `cmd/ls/ls_test.go`, adding differential test cases, and ensuring `go build`, `go test`, and `go vet` all pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs GNU `gls` reference binary\n   - Exit code contract: 0=success, 1=minor problem (file access errors), 2=serious problem (invalid options)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` \n   - GNU ls exit code semantics (ls.c:5638 exit(status), EXIT_FAILURE=2 for bad options at ls.c:2026)\n   - LC_ALL=C for locale-consistent differential testing\n   - The cobbler orchestrator manages git; no git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml** (read in full)\n     - Contains the full SRD specification. R4.1-R4.4 are at lines 175-193.\n     - R4.1: Exit 0 on success\n     - R4.2: Exit 1 on minor problems (file not found, permission denied), still list remaining entries, print diagnostic to stderr\n     - R4.3: Exit 2 on serious problems (invalid command-line option). References ls.c:5638 and ls.c:2026\n     - R4.4: Install SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` using signal.Notify with buffered channel\n\n   - **cmd/ls/main.go** (read in full, 881 lines)\n     - Key finding: SIGPIPE handler already installed at line 77: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n     - Key finding: Invalid options already exit 2 (lines 107, 190, 205)\n     - **BUG FOUND**: `classifyPaths()` at line 257 sets `*exitCode = 2` for file access errors — should be `1` per R4.2\n     - **BUG FOUND**: `listDir()` at line 282 returns `2` for directory open failure — should be `1` per R4.2\n     - **BUG FOUND**: `writeLongFiles()` at line 639 returns `2` for file access failure — should be `1` per R4.2\n     - **BUG FOUND**: `writeLongDir()` at line 670 returns `2` for file access failure — should be `1` per R4.2\n     - The `run()` function at line 221 initializes `exitCode := 0` and uses `maxCode()` to track the worst exit code\n     - `main()` at line 76-83 calls `os.Exit(run(paths, opts))`\n\n   - **cmd/ls/ls_test.go** (read in full, 343 lines)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gls\")`\n     - Has test for `unknown-long-option` with ExitCode: 2 and `unknown-short-option` with ExitCode: 2\n     - Missing: test for exit code 1 on nonexistent file argument\n     - Missing: test for exit code 0 on successful listing (implicitly tested but not explicitly)\n     - Missing: test for mixed valid/invalid paths (some accessible, some not)\n     - Has normalizer for binary name differences between `ls` and `gls`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only read operations were performed before the summary was requested.\n   - Key bugs identified in existing code but not yet fixed:\n     - Exit code 2 used where exit code 1 should be used for file access errors (4 locations in main.go)\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R4.4 (SIGPIPE) is already implemented\n   - Identified that R4.3 (exit 2 for invalid options)